> If you get a djinni, the potion isn't identified.  dodrink() checks
> milky and smoky potions for ghosts and djinn, respectively.  If neither
> occurs, it calls dopotion(), which calls peffects(), which sets flags
> that dopotion() uses to determine whether to identify the potion or not.
> 
> If a djinni pops out, dopotion() doesn't get called, so the potion
> doesn't get IDed.
> 
> If this isn't in the spoilers, maybe it should be, but I don't think
> it's crucial.  It's pretty intuitive that if the djinni pops out, you
> didn't witness or feel the potion's effects, so there's no way for you
> to ID anything but its description.

